  "id": "texture-perception",
  "term": "texture perception",
  "definition": "Texture perception is the haptic sensing of a surface’s textured pattern through touch. In the supplied source, it is described as depending on active finger movement, with more accurate perception of oriented, grooved textures when movements run more nearly across the grooves rather than along them because this provides stronger temporal cues.",
